   --- §32.1.4 (cited for ℛ(X) ⊆ ∏ Aᵢ(X) / cannot be repaired from inside) L8963–L8996
   L8963 ### 32.1.4 What this book names before anyone tells it
   L8964  A closed index admits nothing it lacks, so a *closed* index names nothing unidentified. **This book is
   L8965  not one index but six, and only two of them are closed.** Asked what it can determine before an input
   L8966  is given, the answer is a count:
   L8967 
   L8968   index                            coordinates   E     cells named and unoccupied
   L8969   Λ, the object                              8   0     —
   L8970   Appendix D, fibred by kind × language     16   0     —
   L8971   Appendix D, unfibred                       3   4     four
   L8972   Appendix E (Q), fibred by domain           4   0     —
   L8973   Appendix E (Q), unfibred                   4   1     one
   L8974   Appendix F, the numbers                    3  33     thirty-three
   L8975   the audit set, at four coordinates         4  17     seventeen
   L8976                                                        **a build readout**
   L8977 
   L8978  **Fifty-five cells are named and nobody has put anything in them.** Each is a combination the
   L8979  structure admits, stated in coordinates already defined, arrived at by computation and not by
   L8980  suggestion. That is what E(X) *is* — §18.6 calls it the prediction budget, and this is the budget
   L8981  unspent.
   L8982 
   L8983  **It has been confirmed three times, which is the only evidence that matters here.** Register 285:
   L8984  audit 19 SEQUENCE occupied a cell E(audits) had listed as admitted and absent, found by a defect
   L8985  rather than proposed. Register 294: PROJECTION did the same. Register 278: E over the book's own
   L8986  decisions located a decision that had been deferred rather than made — the section-level locators for
   L8987  Appendices B and F (then C and G). **In each case the cell was named first and the occupant arrived after.**
   L8988 
   L8989  **And there is a hard boundary, which is the honest half of the answer.** E names cells; it never
   L8990  names a coordinate. Every one of the fifty-five is a combination of values the index already carries,
   L8991  and §17's extension test requires a candidate axis to be *offered* before it can be judged. The book
   L8992  predicted the eleven missing audits and could not have predicted DEPTH, the coordinate that made them
   L8993  nineteen. **An index can tell you what it has not said in the language it has. It cannot tell you what
   L8994  it has no language for**, and that is §22.4's closing result read forward rather than back. Register
   L8995  332.
   L8996 
